From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] luma: status icons from applications and extensions live on the shelf

Linux applications and Shell extensions put status icons in the top panel:
tray icons, hardware monitors, the Save and Cancel menu of a Tiling Shell
layout being edited. Luma has no top panel, so they had nowhere to appear
and the flows that depend on them could not be finished. The shelf now
adopts every panel indicator it does not already place -- including ones
added after it is built -- into the secondary controls island, sized and
coloured like Luma's own controls, visible only while its owner shows it,
with its menu opening from the shelf edge.

Screen sharing and recording indicators drew their icons without the
status icon class and inherited a full-size glyph; they now draw at the
shelf's icon size in GNOME's amber.

--- a/data/theme/luma-shelf.css
+++ b/data/theme/luma-shelf.css
@@ -803,3 +803,36 @@
 .luma-shelf-live-island .luma-shelf-material.luma-surface-glass .luma-live-extension-badge-day { color: #2c343a; }
 .luma-shelf-live-island .luma-shelf-material.luma-surface-frost .luma-live-extension-time,
 .luma-shelf-live-island .luma-shelf-material.luma-surface-glass .luma-live-extension-time { color: rgba(44, 52, 58, 0.62); }
+
+/* Status icons from applications and extensions -- tray icons, hardware
+ * monitors, a layout editor's Save button -- sit with the secondary controls
+ * at the size of Luma's own icons. Their colour follows the shelf material. */
+.luma-shelf-actions-box .luma-shelf-extra .panel-button {
+  min-width: 36px;
+  color: inherit;
+  padding: 0 6px; }
+.luma-shelf-actions-box .luma-shelf-extra .panel-button StIcon {
+  icon-size: 16px; }
+.luma-shelf-actions-box .luma-shelf-extra .panel-button StLabel {
+  font-size: 12px;
+  font-weight: 600; }
+.luma-shelf-actions-box .luma-shelf-extra .panel-button StBoxLayout {
+  spacing: 6px; }
+
+/* Screen sharing and recording draw their own icons without the status-icon
+ * class, so they inherited a full-size glyph. They keep GNOME's amber, which
+ * says the screen is leaving the computer. */
+.luma-shelf-actions-box .screen-sharing-indicator,
+.luma-shelf-actions-box .screen-recording-indicator {
+  padding: 0 10px;
+  color: #f5c26b; }
+.luma-shelf-actions-box .screen-sharing-indicator StBoxLayout,
+.luma-shelf-actions-box .screen-recording-indicator StBoxLayout {
+  spacing: 8px; }
+.luma-shelf-actions-box .screen-sharing-indicator StIcon,
+.luma-shelf-actions-box .screen-recording-indicator StIcon {
+  icon-size: 16px; }
+.luma-shelf-actions-box .screen-recording-indicator StLabel {
+  font-size: 12px;
+  font-weight: 600;
+  font-feature-settings: "tnum"; }
--- a/js/ui/shelf.js
